.TH XD\-SOUND 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-sound \- Sounds and Audio Devices Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-sound
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-sound
is Windows XP's Sounds and Audio Devices Properties (Control Panel), on
the sound server through libpulse (PulseAudio, or PipeWire's PulseAudio
server):
.TP
.B Volume
The default output's volume and mute, and the taskbar's volume icon.
.TP
.B Sounds
The sound scheme: the sounds played for windows, menus, message boxes,
devices, the battery, the Recycle Bin, logon and logoff (libcanberra).
.TP
.B Audio
The default output and input devices.
.TP
.B Hardware
The sound cards.
.PP
The buttons that opened XP's Volume Control (Advanced..., Program
Volume...) open
.BR pavucontrol (1),
which must be installed for them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n :
0 Volume, 1 Sounds, 2 Audio, 3 Hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.BR [Sound] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-control (1),
.BR xd\-message (1)
